The given circuit can be redrawn to identify the equivalent resistance. The central part of the circuit forms a balanced Wheatstone bridge if the diagonal resistors are considered, but here it's a more complex parallel-series combination. Let's redraw the circuit to simplify it.
The two 2 \(\Omega\) resistors in the middle branch are in series, giving 4 \(\Omega\). This 4 \(\Omega\) is in parallel with the top 2 \(\Omega\) and bottom 2 \(\Omega\) resistors. So, the equivalent resistance between A and B is:
